# A root `pnpm install` is now possible (package.json declares the toolchain for
# Vercel/CI). It has no dependencies, so it installs nothing — but pnpm still
# materialises both of these at the root. Neither is authoritative: the only real
# manifest and lockfile are atlas/package.json and atlas# The root lockfile IS tracked. It has no dependencies to lock — it exists so
# Vercel's package-manager detection picks pnpm at the repository root and then
# honours package.json#packageManager. Without it Vercel chose npm, never
# provisioned pnpm 11, and build-site.sh met an ambient pnpm too old to read
# atlas/pnpm-lock.yaml (lockfileVersion 9.0): "Ignoring not compatible lockfile"
# then "Headless installation requires a pnpm-lock.yaml file"..
node_modules/
